  "limits": "A Cell prefix read prepares/selects its index once and returns both candidates and an exact-value lease; ordinary candidate reads use the same refinement implementation. The standalone read_stamp API and repeated count/stamp/candidates sequence are removed. The lease pins the base bucket, not just a refined result, and an empty bucket is distinct from budget rejection. Exact-row invalidation still differs from membership-only projection stamps. Existing work counters do not instrument removed preparation/selection calls; no allocation or speed claim. Cache scope invalidation and other query/index lifetimes remain.",
